@startuml
title Getting an account onchain — counterfactual on both sides, for different reasons
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam activityDiamondBackgroundColor #EEF5FF
skinparam activityDiamondBorderColor #4A78B5
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #F5F9FF
skinparam noteBorderColor #4A78B5

start
if (which stack?) then (ERC-4337)
  :derive the address with CREATE2
  from the factory, the implementation
  and the salt;<<#DDE9F8>>
  :fund the address before
  any code exists;
  :first UserOperation carries
  initCode;<<#DDE9F8>>
  :SenderCreator deploys the
  account, then validation runs;
  note right
    The factory must be staked at
    the EntryPoint, or the bundler
    will not accept the operation.
  end note
else (Aztec)
  :derive the address as
  hash(public_keys_hash,
  partial_address);<<#DDE9F8>>
  :receive notes at the address
  before any code exists;
  note right
    The keys are inside the address,
    so the address itself is what a
    sender encrypts to.
  end note
  :deploy and initialise, paying
  through a fee-paying contract
  if the account holds nothing;<<#DDE9F8>>
  if (private-only account?) then (yes)
    :initialisation is enough;
  else (no)
    :public deployment
    is also required;
  endif
endif
:account can send transactions;
stop
@enduml
